My original question:

>Hello Admins !
>
>I=B4ll connect a modem (noname) to my Alpha 4000/100 under digital Unix
4.0!=20
>Does anyone know how ?? Which files must i edit ? Can i configure the
>serial port to 115k boud ?
>
>Many thanks for your help in advance !!
>
>Andy
>
>Sysadmin

Thanx to the following:

Bernt Christandl <beb@mpe.mpg.de>
Natalia Salzberg <natalia@stn-atlas.com.au>

The answer was simple. Here are the bests.

Look at the following URLs:

>>http://www.ornl.gov/cts/archives/mailing-lists/
>>ftp://ftp.ornl.gov/pub/archives/mailing_lists/
>>http://www-archive.stanford.edu/lists/alpha-osf-managers.html
>>http://www.rosat.mpe-garching.mpg.de/mailing-lists/Alpha-OSF-Managers/
>>(this latter address will soon(?) change to www.xray.mpe.mpg.de...)

Or like this:

>>If you look at modem(7) man page, you'll see very detailed info on how
>>to do it.  The gist of it is that you make a getty or uugetty entry in
>>your /etc/inittab file that looks something like:
>>
>>modm:23:respawn:/usr/lib/uucp/uugetty -r /dev/tty00 MODEM vt100
>>
>>and you need to add an entry in the /etc/gettydefs if you're using getty
>>or in the /etc/uugettydefs if you're using uugetty for that MODEM
>>reference.  Mine looks like:
>>
>>MODEM # B38400 HUPCL CS8 # B38400 CS8 SANE IXANY TAB3 HUPCL #login:
>>#MODEM19200
>>
>>To know what this means see the gettydefs(4) man pages.

Many thanx to all others, too !!!

Bye
Andreas

Sysadmin

