Subject: SUMMARY: rc.local equivalent
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078620310548


Hi,

Earlier today I asked,

"We used to run Ultrix 4.3, now we run DEC Unix 4.0.  In DEC Unix, what is
the equivalent file of Ultrix's rc.local file?"

I received several answers, all of them being helpful.  The common
generalization is that there is no one DEC Unix file that is equivalent to
Ultrix's rc.local file, rather a collection of DEC Unix files that
encompass what Ultrix's rc.local file used to.  Such DEC Unix files are:

/sbin/rc0.d
/sbin/rc2.d
/sbin/rc3.d
/sbin/init.d
/etc/rc.config
/etc/inittab

