Many thanks to all those people who responded to my request.

  Unfortunately almost all responses were pointing towards a file
permission problem and I verified that all directory, file permissions and
file sizes associated with sendmail were identical to other DU machines
happily running it (and I started from / too!).  Even deleting the
mailertable and domaintable files didn't make this problem go away!

  BTW, I also ran sendmail-8.8.7/test/t_pathconf to test chmod and it
returned "fpathconf claims that chown is safe and fchown agrees" which was
what was expected.  Yes?

  What I did was rebuilt another sendmail.cf file with a completely default
configuration using the cf.m4 and generic-osf1.mc files (I normally add the
Anti-Relaying ruleset and block address ruleset).  The mailertable and
domaintable entries pointed to the /etc directory and of course were
non-existant.  Get this... it ran.  Didn't even complain about their
non-existance.  

  So, although this is a fixed problem, I don't really know why.  :)
Perhaps it has something to do with a sus /usr/local partition?  But other
programs are running fine.

One of life's mysteries!

Thanks,
Damien.

