For all, who answered, here the answer of Olle Eriksson :

The passwd file isn't used directly, but a  hashed binary file. When
changing /etc/passwd you must also run mkpasswd that produced the
hashed file that is used for higher efficiency.

It seems that everybody besides me knows the solution. Sorry for the
simple question.
If there is anybody else who doesn't know here the summary.

There are two solutions :

1. The simplest : use vipw instead of vi

2. The other one, (after you've used vi ):
   run mkpasswd (/etc/passwd) to update the user database

thanks again for all who helped



