Hi Managers.
Thank you for the definite answers.
There is no support for widescsi adressing in DUNIX before the next
major release of DUNIX in summer 98.

---------------------------
This wrote :
Dr. Thomas P. Blinn, UNIX Software Group, Digital Equipment Corporation

In the current release, DIGITAL UNIX provides support for SCSI device
IDs in the range 0-7.  Some people play tricks with the SCSI controller
ID and set it to a value larger than 7, and use a total of 8 device IDs
(0-7).  There are plans to support a wider range of SCSI IDs in a future
release, but it will not be out sooner than next summer.

Sorry..

Tom

